---------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO WORK ON THE GAME (Step-by-Step for Visual Studio)
---------------------------------------------------------

STEP 1: GET THE LATEST CODE (Do this every time you sit down to code)
1. Open HandaKaNaBa.sln in Visual Studio.
2. At the top menu, click 'Git' -> 'Pull'. 
(This downloads everyone else's finished work so you are up to date).

STEP 2: CREATE YOUR SAFE WORKSPACE (Branching)
Before editing:


Check for uncommitted changes in View → Git Changes. Commit or stash them before switching branches.
Click the branch name in the bottom-right corner, or open Git → Manage Branches.
Select the branch you want to work on. If it’s not listed, fetch or create it first.
Confirm the selected branch name appears in the bottom-right corner. Pull the latest changes for that branch.
Edit your assigned files, then use Git Changes to commit and push. Check the branch name once more before committing.
1. At the top menu, click 'Git' -> 'New Branch'.
2. Name it using your role and what you are doing (e.g., "member2-elnino-logic" or "member3-panic-timer").
3. Click 'Create'. (Check the bottom right of Visual Studio—it should now show your new branch name instead of "main").

STEP 3: WRITE YOUR CODE
1. Open YOUR assigned .cs file from the Solution Explorer.
2. Write your code, test it by pressing F5, and make sure it works.
3. DO NOT open or fix your teammate's file. If their code is breaking yours, message them in the group chat.

STEP 4: SAVE AND UPLOAD (Commit & Push)
1. Go to 'View' -> 'Git Changes' (or look at the Git Changes tab on the right).
2. Type a short message about what you did in the text box (e.g., "Added 10-second panic timer").
3. Click the dropdown arrow next to Commit All and select 'Commit All and Push'.

STEP 5: MERGE YOUR WORK (Pull Request)
1. Go to our repository on GitHub.com.
2. You will see a green button that says "Compare & pull request". Click it.
3. Click "Create pull request".
4. If it says "This branch has no conflicts with the base branch", click "Merge pull request" -> "Confirm merge".
5. Your code is now officially in the main game! 

STEP 6: CLEAN UP
1. Back in Visual Studio, look at the bottom right corner. Click your branch name and switch back to "main".
2. Click 'Git' -> 'Pull' to download your newly merged code.
3. You are ready for your next task!
